  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Social Sciences in an Era of transitions and transformation</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Core support to CODESRIA and its strategic plan (2022-2023), which overall goal is to increase the contributions of Africans to the task of understanding, interpreting and addressing key challenges facing the African continent. The thematic priorities are 1) The state and democratization in Africa 2) Economies and Economic Policy in Africa 3) Ecologies and Society in Africa (including issues related to the environment and climate change) and 4) Higher Education Dynamics in Africa. Gender is a cross-cutting issue. CODESRIA offers African scholars (with a specific focus on female researchers) network, research training, funding and possibilities for publishing their work. There are specific budget lines for scholarships and research grants to female researchers, and gender research schools are organized on a regular basis &#x2013; to which African researchers are invited to present and discuss research on various topics related to gender and gender equality i Africa.</narrative>
  </description>
